;; chapter-cites-verified — a chapter section must only cite VERIFIED claims
;; (REQ-KG-003 / REQ-KG-012).
;;
;; Booklogic port of the tbf:ChapterSectionShape sh:sparql constraint in
;; assets/shapes.ttl:
;;   SELECT $this ?claim WHERE {
;;     $this tbf:usesClaim ?claim .
;;     ?claim tbf:status ?status .
;;     FILTER (?status != "verified")
;;   }
;;
;; The :where binds the section id (?focus), joins its :uses-claim-id to a
;; claim's id, and reads that claim's status; the :filter fires when the cited
;; claim's status is NOT "verified". ?focus is bound positive and is the
;; violation focus node. A section citing a verified claim conforms; a section
;; citing a proposed/disputed/etc. claim fires.
;;
;; The :message and :path are taken EXACTLY from the sh:sparql shape and the C0.2
;; golden (tests/golden/kg/shacl_report_violating.json): the sh:sparql node has
;; an sh:message but no sh:path, so pyshacl reports an empty path "".
;;
;; DATA SOURCE NOTE: no production projector emits chapter-section rows yet
;; (project_ledger loads :chapter-section empty, like :chapter-wiki-ref), so this
;; constraint clears on the bermuda workspace. The violating parity test loads
;; synthetic rows directly. A real chapter-section projector is future work.
(defconstraint :chapter-cites-verified
  :message "Chapter sections must only cite verified claims."
  :path ""
  :where [[?s :chapter-section/id ?focus]
          [?s :chapter-section/uses-claim-id ?claim-id]
          [?c :claim/id ?claim-id]
          [?c :claim/status ?status]]
  :filter [[!= ?status "verified"]])
